<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Cognition ability: the reflex (autonomy, then the decision
  layer) -> intuition -> reasoning cascade, with cancellation and step
  timeouts. The body (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) invokes it
  as its child "cognition" and sends it one bot.ability.cognition.input per
  processing turn; it answers that turn with exactly one of
  bot.ability.cognition.output {turn, output} or bot.ability.failed
  {message, turn, input}, and acknowledges bot.ability.cognition.cancel {turn}
  with bot.ability.cognition.cancelled {turn}.

    idle { awake -rest_after_ms without input-> resting { consolidating
           -> consolidated } } -input-> processing { running_autonomy, after_autonomy,
                               running_decision, after_decision,
                               running_intuition, running_reasoning,
                               completing, failing,
                               cancelling { autonomy, decision, intuition,
                                            reasoning, acknowledging } }
                               -> idle

  Stages: each stage is an SCXML child invoked per turn inside its substate
  (abilities/autonomy/autonomy.scx, abilities/intuition/intuition.scx,
  abilities/reasoning/reasoning.scx, in sibling directories) with the turn as <param>s; it answers through its top-level
  final state's <donedata>, received here as done.invoke.<stage> (the
  invoke ids are the stage names; the substates are running_<stage>):
  {turn, handled, selected?, acted?, reason?, confidence_tuner?, failed?}. Leaving a stage's
  substate cancels it (SCXML 6.4). Handled ends the turn with the stage's
  selections as the output; unhandled goes on to the next stage. Reflex is
  one stage of two layers: the bot's behaviors (autonomy: it gets the stimulus and the
  database, runs the learned behaviors the stimulus triggers, and always
  passes the turn on without a database), then the decision layer (the
  decision service over what they left unhandled,
  abilities/intuition/intuition.scx, the invoke "decision"). The decision
  layer's confidence tuner state ({mean, var, n}) is
  passed in by <param> and kept from the donedata.

  Intuition (the chat tier, decision D144): when the body gives an
  intuition_model (null composes none), abilities/reasoning/reasoning.scx
  is invoked again as the stage "intuition" (its <param> tier) on that
  model, and offered the deliberative handoff,
  bot.ability.reasoning.input: this ability's own offer (its transitions,
  which only log, are what <decision:choice> reads into handoff), tagged
  with this session as its target and added to the turn's choices for
  intuition only, never offered to the body. Intuition selecting it sends
  its other selections and hands the turn on to reasoning with them as
  acted (cognition.stage "intuition unhandled (handoff)"). Its context fit
  learns its own bytes_per_token.

  The order: after_autonomy and after_decision are eventless. The decision
  layer takes the turn unless the turn perceives a handed-back failure of
  reflex or intuition, which only a later stage can perceive (decision
  D140). Intuition takes it when composed, unless the decision layer's
  pass chose reasoning (its donedata's hand_to, decision D150) or the turn
  perceives a handed-back failure of intuition. The decision layer is told the tiers
  its pass may name (its hand_ons param: intuition when composed, then
  reasoning), the bounds' max_context_tokens, and the decision model's
  bytes_per_token, which its donedata teaches and this document keeps
  across turns as it keeps reasoning's.

  Failures: a decision layer or an intuition that fails (its failed
  donedata, or error.communication.<stage>) hands the same turn on to the
  next stage, logged as cognition.cascaded {stage: "reflex" or
  "intuition", reason} (decision D140). Autonomy or reasoning failing fails the
  turn: failing answers bot.ability.failed, and hands the failure back
  to the body as a perceived bot.ability.cognition.step.failed (below).

  Self and recent turns (through the body, which relays them): until the identity has told the
  bot's name (bot.ability.identity.named), every entry into idle sends
  bot.ability.identity.ask {} to the parent;
  the name, the persona's traits and description
  (bot.ability.persona.output) and the short-term register's recent
  turns (bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output, which the body reads
  as each turn starts) are kept, and intuition and reasoning are given
  the self (its name only once told) and the recent turns for their
  prompts.

  Dispatch: each stage sends its own selections (decision D113): a
  decision layer that escalates for low confidence sends its environment
  actions before the turn goes on to reasoning, and names them in its donedata's acted, as the chat intuition tier names
  what it sent before its handoff (decision D144). The turn's acted is what earlier
  stages dispatched before they passed it on; the turn's output, and the
  reflection's cognition_output, is the acted followed by the handling
  stage's selections. Reasoning is told it (its <param> acted) and
  renders it in its prompt's situation as a fact of the turn, never as an
  instruction.

  Step timeouts (decisions D101 and D140): each stage
  substate arms two bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out timers and
  cancels both on exit: one of inactivity (child_operation_timeout_ms)
  and a backstop
  (child_operation_ceiling_ms) for the stage as a whole. A tier's own
  bound (bounds.reflex_timeout_ms for
  autonomy and the decision layer, bounds.intuition_timeout_ms for
  intuition, bounds.reasoning_timeout_ms for reasoning [floppy fields])
  replaces both when the body gives it. Autonomy and the decision layer
  make no streamed call, so their inactivity timer is armed on entry;
  intuition's and reasoning's is armed by the first generate.progress it
  sends on while its streamed reply arrives and re-armed by each one
  after, so a slow model that keeps answering is never cut off, and a
  reply that is not streamed (the run's FLOPPY_STREAM is not true) is
  bounded by the backstop alone. The bounds are <param>s the body passes
  from its bounds param. The transition takes only the timers of the
  stage in hand (_event.sendid, SCXML 5.10.1). A step that times out fails
  only its turn: leaving the stage's substate stops it at once, so
  nothing reboots and every ability keeps its state; failing answers
  bot.ability.failed with the message ("Cognition's reflex step took longer than 30 seconds, so the
  turn failed.") and hands the failure back as a perceived
  bot.ability.cognition.step.timed_out.

  Hand-back: failing sends the body,
  after bot.ability.failed, bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus,
  participants} observing the failed step: {event:
  "bot.ability.cognition.step.failed" or
  "bot.ability.cognition.step.timed_out", data: {message, stage,
  timeout_seconds (timed out only), turn, stimulus}, source:
  "cognition"} (abilities/schemas/ describes each data; stimulus is the
  failed turn's own stimulus envelope, so what went unanswered, and who
  said it, is perceived with the failure), a new turn the
  bot decides on, with the failed turn's participants. stage is the
  tier: reflex (autonomy or the decision layer), intuition or
  reasoning. Bounded: a turn that perceives a handed-back failure itself
  hands nothing back, so a step that keeps failing cannot keep waking the
  bot.

  Cancel: bot.ability.cognition.cancel for the turn in hand moves to
  cancelling/<stage>; leaving the stage's substate already cancelled it, so
  acknowledging sends bot.ability.cognition.cancelled {turn} at once and
  returns to idle. Nothing waits for a teardown (an SCXML invoke cancel is
  synchronous); the body's cancel timer still bounds the acknowledgement.

  Ignore: bot.ability.cognition.ignore is this ability's offer: its
  transitions (in idle and processing, which only log) are what its
  parent reads with <decision:offers>. A selected ignore is the turn's terminal
  product, which only the cognition takes ("cognition only", decision
  D113): the stage that selects it
  sends it here, to its target, and the transition logs it.

  Reflection: a reflection region invokes abilities/reflection/reflection.scx
  as the long-lived child "reflection", beside the turns, and each output is followed by bot.ability.reflection.input
  {turn, cognition_input, cognition_output, self, choices, declined} to it (choices
  the turn's, which a learned behavior's live-turn check holds its
  selections to, decision D221, and declined the learned behaviors
  autonomy ran that declined the turn, decision D230), and each failed or
  cancelled turn by one with outcome failed (and the failure) or cancelled
  and no output, which reflection only remembers (decision D139); a
  bot.ability.persona.revise reflection selects goes to the body, for the
  persona (decision D145); its
  bot.ability.reflection.output settles the turn, and its
  bot.ability.failed {message} is logged. The reflection takes the
  database path and the model by <param>; with no database (null) it
  logs that its memory is absent and answers at once. A bot.reboot from
  it goes to rebooting, which forwards it to the body; it is the only reboot this ability asks for.

  Routines: the root is a parallel of the turns, the reflection region and
  a routines region that invokes abilities/routines/routines.scx as the
  long-lived child "routines" with the database as <param name="database">.
  A settled reflection, output or failure, sends it
  bot.ability.routines.reconcile; each bot.behavior.tick it sends is
  handed to the body as bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus} (the tick's
  envelope, source "routines"), which the body grants a turn. With no database it runs no routine.

  Learning (decision D149): bot.ability.learning.input, a lesson as its
  teacher put it, is this ability's offer too (its transitions, in idle
  and processing, only log). After the output of a turn that selected
  one, completing sends the long-lived child "learning"
  (abilities/learning/learning.scx, the learning region, with the
  database, the model and the bounds as <param>s)
  bot.ability.learning.lesson {turn, content, media_type,
  cognition_input, cognition_output, participants}: the lesson with the
  turn it was taught on. Its bot.ability.learning.output {lesson,
  lesson_turn, learned, behavior, participants} is handed to the body as
  bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus: {event:
  "bot.ability.learning.output", data: {lesson, lesson_turn, learned,
  behavior}, source: "learning"}, participants}, a turn the bot tells its
  teacher in. Bounded: a turn that perceives a lesson's result or a routine's
  tick sends no lesson of its own (decision D220). Each lesson's result
  reconciles the routines at once, so a routine learned, changed or
  broken starts or stops without waiting for the next reflection.

  Readiness: the start sends bot.ability.ready to the parent, once
  (decision D242). What it offers, the parent reads from its live session
  with <decision:offers>: the events its offerable <data> declares,
  bot.ability.cognition.ignore and
  bot.ability.learning.input (both of no effort), while a transition without
  a cond takes them. The stages are per-turn children that offer nothing.

  Choices: each turn's input carries the body's collected choices (its own
  and every ability's offers, each tagged with the session id of its
  offerer); they go to the decision layer (the decision service's enabled transitions),
  intuition and
  reasoning (its dispatch tool; autonomy's learned behaviors name their
  targets themselves), and each stage sends its selections to their
  targets. A send a stage cannot make (an autonomy candidate's)
  fails the stage, which this ability answers as bot.ability.failed.

  Effort ceilings (decisions D196 and D206): a choice carries the effort its
  offerer declares (its offerable <data>; 0 without one, so an
  always-offered event such as the ignore is within every ceiling). Each
  stage's substate frames the turn's choices on entry with
  <cognition:within_ceiling> against its tier's ceiling: the decision
  layer's (decision_effort_ceiling, 0) and intuition's
  (intuition_effort_ceiling, 1), each of which the bounds override [floppy
  fields], and reasoning's, the whole frame. The stage is offered only the
  choices within it (tier_choices, without their effort) and is given the
  heavier ones as held (tier_held, {event, description?} once per event,
  its <param> held), which its prompt renders as the <held> block, so it
  can only hand them on: the decision layer by its pass, intuition by the
  deliberative handoff.

  Contracts: the events it takes reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema (never inline). scxml.rs checks them where each event is
  created: a send whose data a schema rejects is not routed and raises
  error.execution in its sender, so conds only correlate (the turn and
  the hop timer, decision D81). A child that fails after it started
  raises error.communication.<invokeid>, so each region takes only its
  own child's failure by name. The stages' donedata is not checked by scxml.rs, so the
  done.invoke conds also check its turn and shape.

  Rest (decisions D195 and D205): every entry into idle starts in awake,
  which arms awake.after for rest_after_ms (the bounds' rest_after_ms
  [floppy field], else this document's default, 5 minutes: the short-term
  register's recency window, after which no exchange is recent, so rest
  never competes with a live one). When it fires with no input meanwhile,
  the cognition rests: resting logs cognition.rest "resting" and invokes
  abilities/consolidation/consolidation.scx as its child "consolidation"
  with the database and the bounds, which reinforces the people memory holds and merges
  duplicates, one guarded transaction per step; its done.invoke donedata
  {folded, merged, steps, failed, reason} is logged as
  cognition.consolidated, and the cognition stays at rest (consolidated)
  until input. Any bot.ability.cognition.input leaves rest at once
  (cognition.rest "awake"): it is taken as a normal turn, and leaving rest
  cancels a consolidation in progress, whose open transaction commits
  nothing (each step is one transaction, so nothing is half-written).
  What idle takes besides input (a cancel, the ignore, the handoff, the
  identity's name, the persona, the recent turns) leaves rest as it is.

  Bindings: the bot, cognition, decision and processing namespace packages; the stages bind their own
  services (the decision layer: decision with TYPESAFE_API_KEY and
  TYPESAFE_BASE_URL; reasoning: generate with FLOPPY_API_KEY and
  FLOPPY_BASE_URL). The model is the body's (a <param> of the body's
  invoke), else the default below, and goes to reasoning; the
  intuition_model goes to intuition.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:cognition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/cognition"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="cognition" initial="alive">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="model" expr="'Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next'"/>
    <!-- The chat tier's model (decision D144): null composes no intuition
         tier. -->
    <data id="intuition_model" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The memory database file, for autonomy, reasoning, reflection and routines (null: no memory). -->
    <data id="database" expr="null"/>
    <!-- A stage's inactivity bound and its backstop (decision D101). -->
    <data id="child_operation_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="child_operation_ceiling_ms" expr="240000"/>
    <!-- How long idle stays awake with no input before it rests and memory
         consolidates (decisions D195 and D205): the short-term register's
         recency window, 5 minutes (the bounds' rest_after_ms overrides
         it). -->
    <data id="rest_after_ms" expr="300000"/>
    <!-- The decision layer's own bound on its decision. A decision not made in time cascades; the
         reflex tier's step bound (bounds.reflex_timeout_ms), when shorter,
         fails the turn first (decision D140). -->
    <data id="decision_timeout_ms" expr="20000"/>
    <!-- The bounds the body's bounds param overrides (its <param>): these
         two, each tier's own (reflex_timeout_ms, intuition_timeout_ms,
         reasoning_timeout_ms), the effort ceilings
         (decision_effort_ceiling, intuition_effort_ceiling), and
         reflection's revising_timeout_ms and revising_ceiling_ms. -->
    <data id="bounds" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The turn in hand. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="participants" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The learned behaviors autonomy ran this turn that declined it,
         for reflection (decision D230). -->
    <data id="declined" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Each tier's effort ceiling (decision D206): the decision layer and
         intuition are offered only the choices whose effort (0 when its
         offerer declares none) is at most theirs, and the heavier ones are
         rendered as held, so they can only hand them on; reasoning's
         ceiling is the whole frame. The bounds' decision_effort_ceiling and
         intuition_effort_ceiling override them. -->
    <data id="decision_effort_ceiling" expr="0"/>
    <data id="intuition_effort_ceiling" expr="1"/>
    <!-- The stage in hand's frame: its choices and what is held from it. -->
    <data id="tier_choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="tier_held" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The bot's environment this turn (decision D106), for reasoning's
         prompt and the decision layer's instructions. -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The decision layer's confidence tuner. -->
    <data id="confidence_tuner" expr="({mean: 70, var: 100, n: 0})"/>
    <!-- The stage in hand: its name, hop timers, and answer. -->
    <data id="stage" expr="null"/>
    <data id="hop_timer" expr="null"/>
    <data id="ceiling_timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- What earlier stages dispatched before they passed the turn on, and
         the turn's output. -->
    <data id="acted" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The percepts the acted were for, when a stage named them (null:
         the turn's one stimulus). -->
    <data id="acted_percepts" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Reasoning's context fit (decision D143):
         the request bytes a token, 3 until a reply's usage teaches it
         fewer, kept here across turns and passed to each reasoning. -->
    <data id="bytes_per_token" expr="3"/>
    <!-- The same for the intuition tier's model and the decision layer's. -->
    <data id="intuition_bytes_per_token" expr="3"/>
    <data id="decision_bytes_per_token" expr="3"/>
    <!-- The tier the decision layer's pass chose for the turn (its
         donedata's hand_to; null: the next composed one). -->
    <data id="hand_to" expr="null"/>
    <data id="selected" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The failed step: its message, and the stimulus handed back. -->
    <data id="failure" expr="null"/>
    <data id="step" expr="null"/>
    <data id="reboot_reason" expr="null"/>
    <!-- A routine tick's stimulus envelope, for the handoff. -->
    <data id="tick" expr="null"/>
    <!-- What it offers its parent (decision D242), which reads it from its
         live session with <decision:offers>: the ignore, of no effort. -->
    <data id="offerable" expr="({'bot.ability.cognition.ignore': {}, 'bot.ability.learning.input': {}})"/>
    <!-- The deliberative handoff, offered to the intuition tier only. -->
    <data id="handoff" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- What the bot knows of itself: its name, as the identity tells it
         (bot.ability.identity.named, relayed by the body; null until it
         has taken one), and its owner's traits and its own description,
         as the persona tells them (bot.ability.persona.output). -->
    <data id="self" expr="({name: null, traits: [], description: null})"/>
    <!-- Whether the identity has told the name yet (until then it is asked
         on every return to idle). -->
    <data id="name_told" expr="false"/>
    <!-- The short-term register's recent turns, heard and said, as it last
         answered (bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output). -->
    <data id="recent_turns" expr="[]"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="cognition.js"/>

  <parallel id="alive">
  <!-- Ready once, on start (decision D242): idle is entered again after
       every turn. -->
  <onentry>
    <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
  </onentry>
  <!-- The identity's answer to an ask, and the name after each
       adoption. -->
  <transition event="bot.ability.identity.named" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.identity.named.json">
    <assign location="self.name" expr="_event.data.name"/>
    <assign location="name_told" expr="true"/>
  </transition>
  <!-- The persona's traits and description, on waking and after each
       revision. -->
  <transition event="bot.ability.persona.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.output.json">
    <assign location="self.traits" expr="_event.data.traits"/>
    <assign location="self.description" expr="personaDescription(_event)"/>
  </transition>
  <!-- The short-term register's answer to a recent_turns read. -->
  <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output.json">
    <assign location="recent_turns" expr="_event.data.turns"/>
  </transition>
  <state id="turns" initial="idle">
  <!-- Waits for the body's turn, awake and then at rest. -->
  <state id="idle" initial="awake">
    <onentry>
      <decision:choice location="handoff" events="bot.ability.reasoning.input"/>
      <processing:model_facing_schema location="handoff"/>
      <!-- Not yet told its name: ask the identity, through the body, on
           every return to idle until it answers. -->
      <if cond="!name_told">
        <send event="bot.ability.identity.ask" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="({})"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json"
                target="processing">
      <assign location="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      <assign location="stimulus" expr="_event.data.stimulus"/>
      <assign location="focus" expr="inputFocus(_event)"/>
      <assign location="focus_candidates" expr="inputFocusCandidates(_event)"/>
      <assign location="participants" expr="inputParticipants(_event)"/>
      <assign location="choices" expr="inputChoices(_event)"/>
      <assign location="environment" expr="inputEnvironment(_event)"/>
      <assign location="declined" expr="[]"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Nothing in flight: acknowledge at once. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.cognition.cancelled" target="#_parent">
        <param name="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.ignore" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.ignore.json">
      <log label="cognition.ignore" expr="'idle'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.learning.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.learning.input.json">
      <log label="cognition.lesson" expr="'idle'"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The deliberative handoff is this ability's call surface: the
         intuition tier never sends it. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.reasoning.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.reasoning.input.json">
      <log label="cognition.handoff" expr="'idle'"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- No input for rest_after_ms: rest. -->
    <state id="awake">
      <onentry>
        <send id="rest-after" event="awake.after" delayexpr="restDelay()"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="rest-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="awake.after" target="resting"/>
    </state>
    <!-- At rest memory consolidates; input leaves rest at once, which
         cancels the consolidation. -->
    <state id="resting" initial="consolidating">
      <onentry>
        <log label="cognition.rest" expr="'resting'"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <log label="cognition.rest" expr="'awake'"/>
      </onexit>
      <state id="consolidating">
        <invoke id="consolidation" type="scxml" src="../consolidation/consolidation.scx">
          <param name="database" expr="database"/>
          <param name="bounds" expr="bounds"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.consolidation" target="consolidated">
          <log label="cognition.consolidated" expr="consolidatedLog(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.communication.consolidation" target="consolidated">
          <log label="cognition.consolidated" expr="consolidationFailedLog(_event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <state id="consolidated"/>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- One turn of the cascade. -->
  <state id="processing" initial="running_autonomy">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="acted" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="acted_percepts" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="hand_to" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="step" expr="null"/>
      <log label="cognition" expr="processingLog()"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.ignore" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.ignore.json">
      <log label="cognition.ignore" expr="turnLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A lesson is taken after the turn's output (completing). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.learning.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.learning.input.json">
      <log label="cognition.lesson" expr="turnLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.reasoning.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.reasoning.input.json">
      <log label="cognition.handoff" expr="turnLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A step that does not answer in time fails only its turn: leaving
         its substate stops it. The
         transition is internal, so processing's onentry does not run again
         and reset the failure. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out.json"
                cond="isChildHopTimeout(_event)" type="internal" target="failing">
      <log label="cognition.hop.timed_out" expr="hopTimeoutLog(_event)"/>
      <assign location="step" expr="timedOutStep(_event)"/>
      <assign location="failure" expr="step.data.message"/>
    </transition>

    <state id="running_autonomy">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="stage" expr="'autonomy'"/>
        <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="hopDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
        <send idlocation="ceiling_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="ceilingDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <cancel sendidexpr="ceiling_timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="autonomy" type="scxml" src="../autonomy/autonomy.scx">
        <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        <param name="input" expr="processingInput()"/>
        <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json"
                  cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="cancelling_autonomy"/>
      <transition event="done.invoke.autonomy" cond="isHandled(_event)" target="completing">
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="'autonomy handled'"/>
        <assign location="selected" expr="handledOutput(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.autonomy" cond="isUnhandled(_event)" target="after_autonomy">
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="stageLog('autonomy unhandled', _event)"/>
        <assign location="declined" expr="declinedCandidates(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted_percepts" expr="perceptsAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted" expr="actedAfter(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.autonomy" cond="matchesStageOutput(_event)" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="stageFailure(_event)"/>
        <assign location="step" expr="failedStep(failure)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.autonomy" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="stageRunFailure('autonomy', _event)"/>
        <assign location="step" expr="failedStep(failure)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The decision layer takes the turn unless it perceives a handed-back
         failure of reflex (decision D140). -->
    <state id="after_autonomy">
      <transition cond="takesDecision()" target="running_decision"/>
      <transition target="after_decision"/>
    </state>

    <state id="running_decision">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="stage" expr="'decision'"/>
        <cognition:within_ceiling location="tier_choices" heldlocation="tier_held" choices="choices"
                                  ceiling="decisionCeiling()"/>
        <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="hopDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
        <send idlocation="ceiling_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="ceilingDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <cancel sendidexpr="ceiling_timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="decision" type="scxml" src="../intuition/intuition.scx">
        <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
        <param name="focus" expr="focus"/>
        <param name="focus_candidates" expr="focus_candidates"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="tier_choices"/>
        <param name="held" expr="tier_held"/>
        <param name="environment" expr="environment"/>
        <param name="recent" expr="recent_turns"/>
        <param name="confidence_tuner" expr="confidence_tuner"/>
        <param name="decision_timeout_ms" expr="decision_timeout_ms"/>
        <param name="hand_ons" expr="handOns()"/>
        <param name="max_context_tokens" expr="contextTokens()"/>
        <param name="bytes_per_token" expr="decision_bytes_per_token"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json"
                  cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="cancelling_decision"/>
      <transition event="done.invoke.decision" cond="isHandled(_event)" target="completing">
        <assign location="confidence_tuner" expr="decisionTuner(_event)"/>
        <assign location="decision_bytes_per_token" expr="decisionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <log label="cognition.tuner" expr="tunerLog()"/>
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="stageLog('decision handled', _event)"/>
        <assign location="selected" expr="handledOutput(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.decision" cond="isUnhandled(_event)" target="after_decision">
        <assign location="confidence_tuner" expr="decisionTuner(_event)"/>
        <assign location="decision_bytes_per_token" expr="decisionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <log label="cognition.tuner" expr="tunerLog()"/>
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="stageLog('decision unhandled', _event)"/>
        <assign location="hand_to" expr="handTo(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted_percepts" expr="perceptsAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted" expr="actedAfter(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- A failing decision layer hands the same turn on (decision D140). -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.decision" cond="matchesStageOutput(_event)" target="after_decision">
        <assign location="confidence_tuner" expr="decisionTuner(_event)"/>
        <assign location="decision_bytes_per_token" expr="decisionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <log label="cognition.tuner" expr="tunerLog()"/>
        <log label="cognition.cascaded" expr="cascadedLog(stageFailure(_event))"/>
        <assign location="acted_percepts" expr="perceptsAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted" expr="actedAfter(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.decision" target="after_decision">
        <log label="cognition.cascaded" expr="cascadedLog(stageRunFailure('decision', _event))"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The intuition tier takes the turn when the bot composes one, the
         decision layer's pass did not choose reasoning, and the turn
         perceives no handed-back failure of intuition. -->
    <state id="after_decision">
      <transition cond="takesIntuition()" target="running_intuition"/>
      <transition target="running_reasoning"/>
    </state>

    <!-- The chat tier (decision D144): reasoning's chart as intuition, on
         its own model, offered the deliberative handoff. -->
    <state id="running_intuition">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="stage" expr="'intuition'"/>
        <cognition:within_ceiling location="tier_choices" heldlocation="tier_held" choices="choices"
                                  ceiling="intuitionCeiling()"/>
        <!-- Its inactivity bound starts with its streamed reply, as
             reasoning's does (decision D101). -->
        <assign location="hop_timer" expr="'unarmed'"/>
        <send idlocation="ceiling_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="ceilingDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <cancel sendidexpr="ceiling_timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="intuition" type="scxml" src="../reasoning/reasoning.scx">
        <param name="tier" expr="'intuition'"/>
        <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
        <param name="focus" expr="focus"/>
        <param name="focus_candidates" expr="focus_candidates"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="intuitionChoices()"/>
        <param name="held" expr="tier_held"/>
        <param name="environment" expr="environment"/>
        <param name="acted" expr="actedFact()"/>
        <param name="self" expr="selfFact()"/>
        <param name="recent" expr="recent_turns"/>
        <param name="max_context_tokens" expr="contextTokens()"/>
        <param name="completion_reserve_tokens" expr="reserveTokens()"/>
        <param name="bytes_per_token" expr="intuition_bytes_per_token"/>
        <param name="model" expr="intuition_model"/>
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json"
                  cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="cancelling_intuition"/>
      <transition event="generate.progress">
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="hopDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.intuition" cond="isHandled(_event)" target="completing">
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="'intuition handled'"/>
        <assign location="intuition_bytes_per_token" expr="intuitionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="selected" expr="handledOutput(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- It selected the handoff: the turn goes on to reasoning, carrying
           what it sent first. -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.intuition" cond="isUnhandled(_event)" target="running_reasoning">
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="stageLog('intuition unhandled', _event)"/>
        <assign location="intuition_bytes_per_token" expr="intuitionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="acted" expr="actedAfter(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- A failing intuition hands the same turn on (decision D140). -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.intuition" cond="matchesStageOutput(_event)" target="running_reasoning">
        <log label="cognition.cascaded" expr="cascadedLog(stageFailure(_event))"/>
        <assign location="intuition_bytes_per_token" expr="intuitionBytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.intuition" target="running_reasoning">
        <log label="cognition.cascaded" expr="cascadedLog(stageRunFailure('intuition', _event))"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <state id="running_reasoning">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="stage" expr="'reasoning'"/>
        <!-- Reasoning's ceiling is the whole frame: nothing is held. -->
        <cognition:within_ceiling location="tier_choices" choices="choices"/>
        <!-- Reasoning's inactivity bound starts with its streamed reply's
             first progress (below): until then, and for a reply that is not
             streamed, only the backstop applies (decision D101). -->
        <assign location="hop_timer" expr="'unarmed'"/>
        <send idlocation="ceiling_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="ceilingDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <cancel sendidexpr="ceiling_timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <invoke id="reasoning" type="scxml" src="../reasoning/reasoning.scx">
        <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        <param name="stimulus" expr="stimulus"/>
        <param name="focus" expr="focus"/>
        <param name="focus_candidates" expr="focus_candidates"/>
        <param name="choices" expr="tier_choices"/>
        <param name="environment" expr="environment"/>
        <param name="acted" expr="actedFact()"/>
        <param name="self" expr="selfFact()"/>
        <param name="recent" expr="recent_turns"/>
        <param name="max_context_tokens" expr="contextTokens()"/>
        <param name="completion_reserve_tokens" expr="reserveTokens()"/>
        <param name="bytes_per_token" expr="bytes_per_token"/>
        <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json"
                  cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="cancelling_reasoning"/>
      <!-- Reasoning's streamed reply is arriving: the inactivity bound
           starts, or starts over (decision D101). -->
      <transition event="generate.progress">
        <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.cognition.child.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="hopDelay()">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.reasoning" cond="isHandled(_event)" target="completing">
        <log label="cognition.stage" expr="'reasoning handled'"/>
        <assign location="bytes_per_token" expr="bytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="selected" expr="handledOutput(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.reasoning" cond="matchesStageOutput(_event)" target="failing">
        <assign location="bytes_per_token" expr="bytesPerTokenAfter(_event)"/>
        <assign location="failure" expr="stageFailure(_event)"/>
        <assign location="step" expr="failedStep(failure)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.reasoning" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="stageRunFailure('reasoning', _event)"/>
        <assign location="step" expr="failedStep(failure)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The turn's answer. -->
    <state id="completing">
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.cognition.output" target="#_parent">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="output" expr="selected"/>
        </send>
        <send event="bot.ability.reflection.input" target="#_reflection">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="cognition_input" expr="cognitionInput()"/>
          <param name="cognition_output" expr="selected"/>
          <param name="self" expr="selfFact()"/>
          <param name="choices" expr="choices"/>
          <param name="declined" expr="declined"/>
        </send>
        <!-- A lesson the turn selected goes to the learning with the turn
             (decision D149), unless the turn perceives a lesson's result
             or a routine's tick (decision D220);
             last: a send that fails ends the rest of this block. -->
        <if cond="perceivesLessonOrTick()">
          <log label="cognition.lesson" expr="'bounded'"/>
        <elseif cond="hasLesson()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.learning.lesson" target="#_learning">
            <content expr="turnLesson()"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="idle"/>
    </state>
    <!-- The turn failed: answer it, then hand the failed step back to be
         perceived, unless the turn was itself perceiving one. -->
    <state id="failing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="cognition.failed" expr="failure"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="failure"/>
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="input" expr="processingInput()"/>
        </send>
        <if cond="perceivesFailure()">
          <log label="cognition.handed_back" expr="'bounded'"/>
        <else/>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
            <param name="stimulus" expr="step"/>
            <param name="participants" expr="participants"/>
          </send>
        </if>
        <!-- The failed turn is remembered (decision D139), last: a send that
             fails ends the rest of this block. -->
        <send event="bot.ability.reflection.input" target="#_reflection">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="cognition_input" expr="cognitionInput()"/>
          <param name="cognition_output" expr="[]"/>
          <param name="outcome" expr="'failed'"/>
          <param name="failure" expr="failure"/>
          <param name="self" expr="selfFact()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="idle"/>
    </state>

    <!-- Cancelled: leaving the stage's substate cancelled the stage. -->
    <state id="cancelling" initial="cancelling_decision">
      <state id="cancelling_autonomy">
        <onentry><log label="cognition.cancelled" expr="'autonomy'"/></onentry>
        <transition target="acknowledging"/>
      </state>
      <state id="cancelling_decision">
        <onentry><log label="cognition.cancelled" expr="'decision'"/></onentry>
        <transition target="acknowledging"/>
      </state>
      <state id="cancelling_intuition">
        <onentry><log label="cognition.cancelled" expr="'intuition'"/></onentry>
        <transition target="acknowledging"/>
      </state>
      <state id="cancelling_reasoning">
        <onentry><log label="cognition.cancelled" expr="'reasoning'"/></onentry>
        <transition target="acknowledging"/>
      </state>
      <state id="acknowledging">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.cancelled" target="#_parent">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          </send>
          <!-- The cancelled turn is remembered (decision D139). -->
          <send event="bot.ability.reflection.input" target="#_reflection">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
            <param name="cognition_input" expr="cognitionInput()"/>
            <param name="cognition_output" expr="[]"/>
            <param name="outcome" expr="'cancelled'"/>
            <param name="self" expr="selfFact()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition target="idle"/>
      </state>
    </state>
  </state>

  </state>

  <!-- The reflection: a long-lived child that reflects on each turn after
       its output, beside the next turns. -->
  <state id="reflection_region" initial="reflection_running">
    <state id="reflection_running">
      <invoke id="reflection" type="scxml" src="../reflection/reflection.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        <param name="bounds" expr="bounds"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.reflection.output.json">
        <log label="bot.ability.reflection.output" expr="turnLog()"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.routines.reconcile" target="#_routines">
          <content expr="({})"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json">
        <log label="cognition.reflection.failed" expr="_event.data.message"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.routines.reconcile" target="#_routines">
          <content expr="({})"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A persona revision reflection selected (decision D145) goes to the
           body, which passes it to the persona. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.persona.revise" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.persona.revise.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.persona.revise" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- The reflection's reboot: the body restarts this ability. -->
      <transition event="bot.reboot" event:schema="../schemas/bot.reboot.json" target="rebooting">
        <assign location="reboot_reason" expr="_event.data.reason"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.reflection" target="reflection_stopped">
        <log label="cognition.reflection.failed" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="reflection_stopped"/>
  </state>

  <!-- The learning: a long-lived child that learns each lesson a turn
       selected, and whose result goes to the body, which grants it a turn
       (decision D149). -->
  <state id="learning_region" initial="learning_running">
    <state id="learning_running">
      <invoke id="learning" type="scxml" src="../learning/learning.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="model" expr="model"/>
        <param name="bounds" expr="bounds"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.learning.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.learning.output.json">
        <!-- The result first: with the routines stopped the reconcile's
             send fails and ends the block. -->
        <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
          <param name="stimulus" expr="lessonStimulus(_event)"/>
          <param name="participants" expr="_event.data.participants"/>
        </send>
        <send event="bot.ability.routines.reconcile" target="#_routines">
          <content expr="({})"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.learning" target="learning_stopped">
        <log label="cognition.learning.failed" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="learning_stopped"/>
  </state>

  <!-- The routines: a long-lived child whose ticks go to the body, which
       grants each one a turn. -->
  <state id="routines_region" initial="routines_running">
    <state id="routines_running">
      <invoke id="routines" type="scxml" src="../routines/routines.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.behavior.tick" event:schema="../schemas/bot.behavior.tick.json">
        <assign location="tick" expr="({})"/>
        <assign location="tick.event" expr="_event.name"/>
        <assign location="tick.data" expr="_event.data"/>
        <assign location="tick.source" expr="'routines'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
          <param name="stimulus" expr="tick"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.communication.routines" target="routines_stopped">
        <log label="cognition.routines.failed" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="routines_stopped"/>
  </state>
  </parallel>

  <!-- Waits for the body to restart this ability (it re-enters live). -->
  <state id="rebooting">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.reboot" target="#_parent">
        <param name="reason" expr="reboot_reason"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <!-- The turn is lost: acknowledge a cancel for it at once. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancel.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.cognition.cancelled" target="#_parent">
        <param name="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
